<configuration>
  <property name="LOG_LEVEL" value="${LOG_LEVEL:-INFO}" />

  <!-- HEL-1128: LOG_FORMAT selects the console appender WITHOUT using logback's
       <if> conditional-processing construct. Local reproduction (real
       Dockerfile + real throwaway Postgres, both with and without <if> in this
       exact fat-jar build) probe-confirmed that ANY use of <if> here — whether
       wrapping <root> at the top level, or nested inside <root> around just the
       <appender-ref> — causes Joran to report a clean "End of configuration"
       with no ERROR status, yet the root logger ends up with NO appender
       attached at runtime: `-Dlogback.debug=true` surfaced "No appenders
       present in context [default] for logger [...]" for Pekko's very first
       log call, and zero application/Flyway output ever reached stdout
       afterward, identically on both the LOG_FORMAT=json and LOG_FORMAT-unset
       branches — proving the failure is in <if> processing itself in this
       fat-jar build, not in which branch is selected. Removing <if> entirely
       (both appenders declared unconditionally; the SELECTED appender's name
       is chosen via plain property substitution in `<appender-ref ref="...">`)
       was probe-confirmed, with the same local repro, to restore output on
       both LOG_FORMAT values. See design.md for the full transcript.

       HEL-1128 round 2 (skeptic-final-1.md REFUTE): a plain `${LOG_FORMAT:-plain}`
       substitution only matches the literal string "json" exactly — `JSON`,
       `Json`, or a typo silently left ROOT with no appender at all (the same
       silent-logging-loss defect this ticket exists to fix, just for a
       different set of input values), and regressed the case-insensitive
       fallback contract in openspec/specs/structured-json-logging/spec.md and
       CLAUDE.md's LOG_FORMAT row. Fixed with a `<define>` (a custom
       `PropertyDefiner`, com.helio.logging.LogFormatPropertyDefiner) that
       normalizes LOG_FORMAT case-insensitively into exactly "json" or "plain"
       as plain JVM code, entirely outside logback's appender-attachment
       processing — so there is still zero conditional-processing construct
       anywhere in the appender-attachment path itself, only in computing
       which already-resolved string value gets substituted into
       `ref="${LOG_APPENDER}"`. Probe-confirmed (same local repro) that
       LOG_FORMAT=JSON now gives JSON output and LOG_FORMAT=garbage gives
       plain-text output, neither one silence. -->
  <define name="LOG_APPENDER" class="com.helio.logging.LogFormatPropertyDefiner" />

  <appender name="json" class="ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender">
    <!-- Structured JSON output for production (Cloud Logging). LogstashEncoder
         includes MDC entries by default. The level field is renamed to a
         top-level `severity` field so Cloud Logging classifies entries. -->
    <encoder class="net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder">
      <fieldNames>
        <level>severity</level>
      </fieldNames>
    </encoder>
  </appender>

  <appender name="plain" class="ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender">
    <!-- Human-readable plain-text output (dev/local default). -->
    <encoder>
      <pattern>%d{HH:mm:ss.SSS} %-5level [%thread] %logger{36} - %msg%n</pattern>
    </encoder>
  </appender>

  <root level="${LOG_LEVEL}">
    <appender-ref ref="${LOG_APPENDER}" />
  </root>
</configuration>
